<title>BRAZIL: FORECAST- Consensus survey of Brazilian indicators.</title>
<headline>FORECAST- Consensus survey of Brazilian indicators.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are consensus forecasts on Brazilian economic indicators according to a Reuters survey of eight Sao Paulo and Rio de Janeiro brokerages and research firms. Also included are current market rates for dollar and interest rate futures over the next three months.</p>
<p>Each is updated twice monthly after the release of export figures early in the month and trade balance later in the month. </p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>****Brazil Indicators - January Consensus Forecast****</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    INDICATOR	 PERIOD    AVG FORCST   MEDIAN   PRVS MONTH</p>
<p>    CPI (Fipe)	   Jan	1.09 pct   1.05 pct   0.17 pct</p>
<p>    PPI (IPA-M/FGV)    Jan	1.88 pct   2.00 pct   1.23 pct</p>
<p>    Inflation (IGP-M)  Jan	1.63 pct   1.85 pct   0.73 pct</p>
<p>    Ind Act (IBGE)     Dec	8.06 pct   8.15 pct   n/a</p>
<p>    Trade Balance	Jan     -$903 million  -$965 million -$1.79bln</p>
<p>    Exports		Jan    $3.50 bln   $3.5 bln  $3.789 bln</p>
<p>    Imports		Jan    $4.395 bln  $4.45 bln $5.576 bln</p>
<p>				   *****</p>
<p>	     Brazilian Financial Indicators</p>
<p>	 Futures market rates at January 24 Close</p>
<p>	 January	   February	March</p>
<p>    Real/Dollar	1.0465	    1.0553	1.0645</p>
<p> Monthly Int Rates   1.743 pct	 1.705 pct   1.679 pct</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Notes: Price indicators reflect monthly variation. Industrial activity reflects annual variation. </p>
<p>((--John Miller, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248-5414))</p>
